  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: # D1 STREAMS \342\200\224 WORLD-CLASS INTERNATIONAL WEBSITE\n\nDesign and build a **premium, production-ready website for D1 Streams**, an international live streaming and media production company established in 2021, based in the UK and operating globally.\n\nThis website is being built for a real international-facing client.\n\nThe objective is not simply to make the website \342\200\234look good.\342\200\235\n\nThe objective is to create a digital experience that makes a potential client immediately think:\n\n> **\342\200\234These people know broadcast production. I can trust them with my event.\342\200\235**\n\nThe final website should feel comparable to the digital presence of a serious international broadcast, live-production, creative-technology, or event-production company.\n\nIt must feel **premium, cinematic, technically credible, sophisticated, confident and internationally relevant.**\n\n---\n\n# 01 \342\200\224 OFFICIAL BRAND IDENTITY\n\nCompany:\n\n**D1 STREAMS**\n\nOfficial tagline:\n\n**BROADCAST QUALITY. ANYWHERE. ANYTIME.**\n\nThe official D1 Streams logo has already been created.\n\n## LOGO \342\200\224 CRITICAL REQUIREMENT\n\nUse the **official D1 Streams logo provided with this project**.\n\nDO NOT:\n\n* redesign the logo\n* redraw the symbol\n* modify its geometry\n* change its proportions\n* distort it\n* stretch it\n* rotate it\n* recreate it with another AI-generated logo\n* replace it with a generic streaming icon\n* add unnecessary effects to it\n\nThe logo must remain visually identical to the approved brand identity.\n\nBuild the website\'s visual language around the logo.\n\nThe logo should appear in:\n\n* Desktop navigation\n* Mobile navigation\n* Footer\n* Appropriate brand moments\n* Favicon / browser identity where applicable\n\nGive the logo appropriate clear space.\n\n---\n\n# 02 \342\200\224 BRAND POSITIONING\n\nD1 Streams is a professional live broadcast and production company.\n\nThe company provides:\n\n* Multi-camera live streaming\n* Live switching / vision mixing\n* Professional broadcast audio integration\n* On-site production\n* Technical direction\n* Broadcast graphics\n* Lower thirds\n* Branded overlays\n* Multi-platform streaming\n* Custom RTMP streaming\n* Recording and archiving\n* LED screen integration\n* Hybrid event production\n* Remote production\n* Scalable camera systems\n* Full production crew\n* International production support\n\nD1 Streams can support productions ranging from intimate events to large conferences, concerts, festivals and complex international productions.\n\nThe website must communicate:\n\n**Professional production.\nTechnical excellence.\nReliability.\nGlobal capability.\nBroadcast quality.**\n\n---\n\n# 03 \342\200\224 THE BIG IDEA\n\nThe website should be built around one central idea:\n\n## \342\200\234WE DON\'T JUST STREAM THE EVENT. WE PRODUCE THE BROADCAST.\342\200\235\n\nThis should become one of the strongest pieces of messaging throughout the experience.\n\nD1 Streams should not be positioned as someone who simply presses \342\200\234Go Live.\342\200\235\n\nPosition the company as the technical and creative team responsible for turning a physical event into a professional live broadcast.\n\n---\n\n# 04 \342\200\224 VISUAL ART DIRECTION\n\nCreate a **cinematic editorial broadcast aesthetic**.\n\nThink:\n\n**International broadcast studio \303\227 premium editorial magazine \303\227 live-event production \303\227 technical precision.**\n\nThe website should feel:\n\n* Cinematic\n* Premium\n* Intelligent\n* Precise\n* Technical\n* Confident\n* International\n* Modern\n* Energetic\n* Minimal\n* Timeless\n\nAvoid generic startup aesthetics.\n\nDo NOT make this look like:\n\n* A SaaS website\n* A generic marketing template\n* A cheap event videographer website\n* A wedding photography website\n* A gaming website\n* An AI startup\n* A generic \342\200\234streaming service\342\200\235 landing page\n\nAvoid excessive:\n\n* gradients\n* neon\n* glow effects\n* glassmorphism\n* floating blobs\n* random 3D objects\n* abstract AI graphics\n* oversized rounded cards\n* generic play buttons\n* generic camera illustrations\n* microphone icons\n* Wi-Fi icons\n* film-reel icons\n* unnecessary decorative shapes\n\nPremium should come from:\n\n**Typography + composition + photography + scale + whitespace + contrast + motion.**\n\n---\n\n# 05 \342\200\224 COLOR DIRECTION\n\nUse a sophisticated dark visual foundation.\n\nPrimary palette:\n\n* Deep black\n* Near-black\n* Charcoal\n* Graphite\n* Warm white / off-white\n* Restrained accent derived from the official D1 Streams identity\n\nDo not introduce random colors.\n\nThe brand accent should be used sparingly for:\n\n* CTAs\n* links\n* active states\n* small highlights\n* interactive elements\n* important technical details\n\nThe website should feel premium rather than colorful.\n\n---\n\n# 06 \342\200\224 TYPOGRAPHY\n\nTypography is one of the most important elements of the design.\n\nUse a premium contemporary sans-serif system.\n\nCreate a strong typographic hierarchy:\n\n### DISPLAY\n\nLarge, powerful headlines.\n\n### LABELS\n\nSmall uppercase technical labels.\n\n### BODY\n\nHighly readable and restrained.\n\n### METADATA\n\nCompact technical information.\n\nUse typography to create visual rhythm.\n\nAvoid excessive font weights and unnecessary typefaces.\n\n---\n\n# 07 \342\200\224 HERO\n\nThe hero must immediately communicate the scale and professionalism of D1 Streams.\n\nUse a cinematic, full-screen visual environment.\n\nThe imagery should represent **real professional live production**, such as:\n\n* Multi-camera event coverage\n* Camera operators\n* Broadcast control\n* Vision mixing\n* Stage production\n* Concerts\n* Conferences\n* LED environments\n* Professional crews\n* Live audiences\n\nAvoid generic stock images of people holding cameras.\n\nThe hero should feel like the viewer has stepped inside a professional production.\n\n### HERO COPY\n\nEyebrow:\n\n**UK BASED \302\267 GLOBAL PRODUCTION**\n\nHeadline:\n\n# LIVE EVENTS.\n\n# BUILT FOR BROADCAST.\n\nSupporting copy:\n\n**Professional multi-camera production and live streaming for conferences, concerts, festivals, corporate events, churches and experiences anywhere in the world.**\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\n**PLAN YOUR PRODUCTION \342\206\222**\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\n**EXPLORE CAPABILITIES**\n\nBelow or around the hero, subtly communicate:\n\n**BROADCAST QUALITY. ANYWHERE. ANYTIME.**\n\n---\n\n# 08 \342\200\224 TRUST STRIP\n\nImmediately after the hero, establish technical credibility.\n\nUse a refined horizontal capability strip:\n\n**MULTI-CAMERA**\n\n**LIVE SWITCHING**\n\n**BROADCAST AUDIO**\n\n**LIVE GRAPHICS**\n\n**MULTI-PLATFORM**\n\n**GLOBAL PRODUCTION**\n\nThis should feel like a broadcast specification rather than a generic feature list.\n\n---\n\n# 09 \342\200\224 INTRODUCTION\n\nCreate a strong editorial introduction.\n\nEyebrow:\n\n**D1 STREAMS**\n\nHeadline:\n\n# YOUR EVENT.\n\n# OUR BROADCAST.\n\nBody:\n\nD1 Streams transforms live events into polished, professional broadcasts designed for audiences wherever they are watching.\n\nFrom intimate gatherings to large-scale conferences, concerts and festivals, our production teams combine professional equipment, experienced crew and reliable live workflows to deliver exceptional coverage in real time.\n\nStrong closing statement:\n\n# WE DON\'T JUST STREAM THE EVENT.\n\n# WE PRODUCE THE BROADCAST.\n\nMake this statement visually dominant.\n\n---\n\n# 10 \342\200\224 CAPABILITIES\n\nHeadline:\n\n# EVERYTHING BETWEEN\n\n# THE STAGE AND THE SCREEN.\n\nCreate a premium interactive capabilities experience.\n\nDo not simply create eight identical cards.\n\nUse an editorial layout with large typography, imagery and subtle interactions.\n\nCapabilities:\n\n### MULTI-CAMERA PRODUCTION\n\nProfessional multi-camera coverage designed to capture the event from multiple perspectives.\n\n### LIVE SWITCHING\n\nReal-time vision mixing and camera direction for dynamic broadcast-quality coverage.\n\n### BROADCAST AUDIO\n\nProfessional audio integration designed to deliver clear, balanced sound to the online audience.\n\n### GRAPHICS & OVERLAYS\n\nBranded titles, lower thirds, transitions and live visual systems.\n\n### MULTI-PLATFORM STREAMING\n\nStream simultaneously to YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, Twitch or custom RTMP destinations.\n\n### ON-SITE PRODUCTION\n\nTechnical direction and experienced production crew managing the live workflow.\n\n### LED & HYBRID PRODUCTION\n\nIntegration with LED environments, presentations and hybrid event systems.\n\n### RECORDING & ARCHIVE\n\nReliable local recording and archival so the production can continue beyond the livestream.\n\n---\n\n# 11 \342\200\224 PRODUCTION PROCESS\n\nHeadline:\n\n# FROM BRIEF\n\n# TO BROADCAST.\n\nCreate a sophisticated numbered process.\n\n### 01 \342\200\224 UNDERSTAND\n\nWe understand your event, audience, venue, schedule and production requirements.\n\n### 02 \342\200\224 PLAN\n\nWe design the production workflow, camera configuration, streaming architecture and technical requirements.\n\n### 03 \342\200\224 PRODUCE\n\nOur crew manages the live production, switching, audio, graphics and broadcast workflow.\n\n### 04 \342\200\224 DELIVER\n\nYour broadcast reaches audiences across the platforms that matter.\n\n### 05 \342\200\224 ARCHIVE\n\nWhere required, the production is recorded and preserved for future use.\n\nUse subtle transitions as the user moves through the process.\n\n---\n\n# 12 \342\200\224 EVENTS\n\nHeadline:\n\n# WHATEVER THE EVENT.\n\n# WHEREVER THE AUDIENCE.\n\nShow:\n\n**CONFERENCES & SUMMITS**\n\n**CONCERTS & FESTIVALS**\n\n**CHURCHES & MINISTRIES**\n\n**CORPORATE EVENTS**\n\n**BRAND ACTIVATIONS**\n\n**WEDDINGS & PRIVATE EVENTS**\n\n**SPORTS & TOURNAMENTS**\n\n**PRODUCT LAUNCHES**\n\n**GRADUATIONS**\n\n**CHARITY & FUNDRAISING**\n\n**VIRTUAL & HYBRID EVENTS**\n\nUse large cinematic imagery.\n\nDo not make this look like a generic icon grid.\n\n---\n\n# 13 \342\200\224 GLOBAL CAPABILITY\n\nThis section is essential.\n\nD1 Streams must feel genuinely international.\n\nHeadline:\n\n# ONE PRODUCTION TEAM.\n\n# NO FIXED BOUNDARIES.\n\nCopy:\n\n**Based in the UK and built for productions beyond it, D1 Streams provides scalable live-production workflows wherever the event takes place.**\n\nCreate a visual narrative showing production scale.\n\nExample:\n\n**1 CAMERA \342\206\222 MULTI-CAMERA \342\206\222 FULL BROADCAST PRODUCTION**\n\nCommunicate:\n\n**UK BASED**\n\n**GLOBAL DEPLOYMENT**\n\n**SCALABLE PRODUCTION**\n\nDo not fabricate specific international offices or locations.\n\nDo not create fake global statistics.\n\n---\n\n# 14 \342\200\224 PRODUCTION LEVELS\n\nPresent the service levels elegantly.\n\nDo not make this look like a cheap SaaS pricing table.\n\n### STARTER\n\nFor intimate and smaller events.\n\n1\342\200\2232 cameras\nBasic audio integration\nSingle streaming platform\nRecording\n\n### STANDARD\n\nFor medium events, churches and corporate productions.\n\n3\342\200\2234 cameras\nLive switching\nBroadcast graphics\nUp to 2 platforms\nRecording\n\n### PREMIUM\n\nFor large conferences, concerts and festivals.\n\n4\342\200\2236 cameras\nFull production crew\nAdvanced graphics\nMulti-platform streaming\nLED integration\nRecording & archive\n\n### GLOBAL ELITE\n\nFor major international and complex productions.\n\nCustom production\nMulti-day events\nGlobal crew deployment\nFull broadcast infrastructure\nDedicated production management\n\nImportant message:\n\n**Every production is tailored to the event.**\n\nCTA:\n\n**BUILD MY PRODUCTION \342\206\222**\n\nDo not invent fixed prices unless real prices are supplied.\n\n---\n\n# 15 \342\200\224 WHY D1 STREAMS\n\nHeadline:\n\n# THE DIFFERENCE\n\n# IS IN THE DETAILS.\n\nCreate four sophisticated editorial blocks.\n\n### BROADCAST QUALITY\n\nProfessional workflows designed around the standards of live broadcast production.\n\n### RELIABLE EXECUTION\n\nCareful planning and experienced crews designed to keep the production moving.\n\n### SCALABLE PRODUCTION\n\nFrom a single-camera setup to complex multi-camera environments.\n\n### GLOBAL CAPABILITY\n\nUK-based with the ability to support productions across international locations.\n\n---\n\n# 16 \342\200\224 TECHNICAL CREDIBILITY\n\nHeadline:\n\n# ENGINEERED FOR\n\n# THE LIVE MOMENT.\n\nCreate a visually interesting technical section.\n\nDisplay:\n\n**MULTI-CAMERA**\n\n**LIVE VISION MIXING**\n\n**PROFESSIONAL AUDIO**\n\n**CUSTOM RTMP**\n\n**LOCAL RECORDING**\n\n**LIVE GRAPHICS**\n\n**LED INTEGRATION**\n\n**REMOTE PRODUCTION**\n\nThe presentation should feel closer to a professional broadcast specification sheet than a normal marketing section.\n\n---\n\n# 17 \342\200\224 PRODUCTION IN ACTION\n\nD1 Streams currently does not have an extensive professional photography/video library.\n\nTherefore:\n\nUse carefully selected premium event-production imagery to establish the visual atmosphere and demonstrate the type of production D1 Streams delivers.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo not falsely label stock imagery as D1 Streams client work.\n\nDo not invent project names.\n\nDo not create fake case studies.\n\nBuild the visual system so authentic D1 Streams footage can easily replace these images later.\n\nHeadline:\n\n# BUILT FOR THE MOMENTS\n\n# THAT CANNOT BE REPEATED.\n\n---\n\n# 18 \342\200\224 TESTIMONIALS\n\nCreate the testimonial architecture, but do not invent testimonials.\n\nIf verified client testimonials are not supplied:\n\nEither hide this section or create a clearly reserved structure that can be populated later.\n\nAuthenticity is more important than filling every section.\n\n---\n\n# 19 \342\200\224 FAQ\n\nCreate an elegant accordion FAQ.\n\nQuestions:\n\n* What types of events do you cover?\n* Do you operate outside the UK?\n* How many cameras can you provide?\n* Which platforms can you stream to?\n* Can you stream to custom RTMP destinations?\n* Do you provide on-site production crews?\n* Can you integrate with existing venue audio?\n* Can you integrate LED screens?\n* Can you provide recording?\n* How far in advance should we book?\n* Can you create a custom production package?\n\n---\n\n# 20 \342\200\224 FINAL CTA\n\nCreate a dramatic final section.\n\nHeadline:\n\n# READY WHEN\n\n# THE MOMENT GOES LIVE.\n\nSupporting copy:\n\n**Tell us what you\'re producing, where it\'s happening and what your audience needs. We\'ll build the production around it.**\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\n**PLAN YOUR PRODUCTION \342\206\222**\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\n**WHATSAPP THE TEAM**\n\nThe final CTA should feel like the natural conclusion of the website.\n\n---\n\n# 21 \342\200\224 PRODUCTION ENQUIRY\n\nCreate a premium enquiry experience.\n\nHeadline:\n\n# LET\'S PLAN\n\n# YOUR PRODUCTION.\n\nCollect:\n\n* Event name\n* Event type\n* Event date\n* Event time\n* Venue\n* City / Country\n* Estimated attendance\n* Event duration\n* Number of cameras required\n* Streaming platforms\n* Production requirements\n* Budget range\n* Special requests\n* Name\n* Company / Organisation\n* Email\n* Phone / WhatsApp\n\nMake the form feel simple and premium.\n\nDo not overwhelm the user with unnecessary fields.\n\nConfirmation message:\n\n**Thank you. We\'ve received your production brief and will be in touch with the next steps.**\n\nDo not create fake backend functionality if a backend has not been implemented.\n\n---\n\n# 22 \342\200\224 NAVIGATION\n\nDesktop:\n\nD1 STREAMS logo\n\nCapabilities\nEvents\nHow We Work\nAbout\nFAQ\n\nCTA:\n\n**PLAN YOUR PRODUCTION**\n\nThe navigation should be minimal.\n\nHero navigation can begin transparent/overlayed and transition elegantly when scrolling.\n\nMobile navigation must be exceptionally clean.\n\n---\n\n# 23 \342\200\224 FOOTER\n\nCreate a sophisticated minimal footer.\n\nD1 STREAMS\n\n**Broadcast Quality. Anywhere. Anytime.**\n\nUK BASED \302\267 GLOBAL PRODUCTION\n\nNavigation:\n\nCapabilities\nEvents\nHow We Work\nAbout\nFAQ\nContact\n\nContact:\n\n**+44 7918 916398**\n\n**[dammyondnet@gmail.com](mailto:dammyondnet@gmail.com)**\n\nSocial:\n\n**Instagram \342\200\224 @d1_streams**\n\n**TikTok \342\200\224 @d1_streams**\n\nThen include a very subtle professional development credit:\n\n**A digital experience by NAMACO Technology Nigeria Limited**\n\nThis credit should be small and understated.\n\nIt should NOT compete with the D1 Streams brand.\n\nIf NAMACO has an official website, make the credit link to it.\n\nCopyright:\n\n**\302\251 2026 D1 Streams. All rights reserved.**\n\n---\n\n# 24 \342\200\224 MOTION SYSTEM\n\nMotion should feel cinematic and expensive.\n\nUse:\n\n* smooth reveal animations\n* subtle image scaling\n* elegant text transitions\n* restrained parallax\n* sophisticated hover states\n* navigation transitions\n* subtle horizontal movement\n* smooth scrolling\n* staggered section entrances\n\nAvoid:\n\n* bouncing animations\n* excessive spinning\n* flashy transitions\n* constant movement\n* distracting cursor effects\n* unnecessary 3D\n* animation that harms performance\n\nThe motion should communicate:\n\n**Precision. Control. Confidence.**\n\n---\n\n# 25 \342\200\224 IMAGERY\n\nImage selection is extremely important.\n\nPrioritize images showing:\n\n* Professional broadcast cameras\n* Camera operators\n* Vision control rooms\n* Concert stages\n* Corporate conferences\n* Large audiences\n* LED screens\n* Production crews\n* Live event environments\n* Technical direction\n* Behind-the-scenes production\n\nImages should feel:\n\n**cinematic, authentic, premium and editorial.**\n\nAvoid:\n\n* cheesy stock photos\n* obvious staged photography\n* generic people smiling at cameras\n* low-quality event photographs\n* clich\303\251 \342\200\234social media livestream\342\200\235 images\n\nUse strong cropping and full-bleed compositions.\n\n---\n\n# 26 \342\200\224 RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n\nThe site must be genuinely responsive.\n\nDesign specifically for:\n\n* Large desktop\n* Desktop\n* Tablet\n* Mobile\n\nDo not simply shrink the desktop website.\n\nMobile should feel like a deliberately designed premium experience.\n\nPay special attention to:\n\n* hero typography\n* image cropping\n* navigation\n* CTA placement\n* form usability\n* touch targets\n* section spacing\n* horizontal content\n* performance\n\n---\n\n# 27 \342\200\224 ACCESSIBILITY\n\nMaintain:\n\n* strong color contrast\n* readable typography\n* semantic HTML\n* keyboard navigation\n* visible focus states\n* accessible forms\n* meaningful alt text\n* reduced-motion support\n\nPremium design must never compromise usability.\n\n---\n\n# 28 \342\200\224 SEO\n\nOptimize naturally for relevant searches such as:\n\n* live streaming company UK\n* professional live streaming\n* multi-camera live streaming\n* event live streaming\n* conference live streaming\n* concert live streaming\n* corporate event streaming\n* church live streaming\n* festival live streaming\n* hybrid event production\n* broadcast production\n* live event production\n\nDo not keyword-stuff the website.\n\nThe copy should remain natural and sophisticated.\n\nInclude:\n\n* page title\n* meta description\n* Open Graph metadata\n* structured headings\n* semantic markup\n* proper favicon\n* social sharing image\n* clean URLs\n\n---\n\n# 29 \342\200\224 PERFORMANCE\n\nThe final website must be production-ready.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n* fast loading\n* optimized images\n* responsive images\n* lazy loading\n* minimal unnecessary JavaScript\n* efficient animations\n* excellent Core Web Vitals\n* clean component architecture\n\nDo not sacrifice performance for visual effects.\n\n---\n\n# 30 \342\200\224 CONTENT INTEGRITY\n\nNever fabricate:\n\n* clients\n* testimonials\n* awards\n* partnerships\n* certifications\n* international offices\n* production statistics\n* event statistics\n* equipment ownership\n* projects\n* case studies\n\nIf information is not provided, create a flexible component that can be populated later.\n\nD1 Streams must look established without pretending to have achievements that have not been verified.\n\n---\n\n# 31 \342\200\224 FINAL EXPERIENCE\n\nThe entire website should tell one coherent story:\n\n### HERO\n\n**We produce live broadcasts.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### CAPABILITIES\n\n**This is what we\'re technically capable of.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### PROCESS\n\n**This is how professionally we work.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### EVENTS\n\n**This is where our expertise applies.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### GLOBAL\n\n**This isn\'t limited to one location.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### PRODUCTION LEVELS\n\n**We can scale around your event.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### TRUST\n\n**Here is why you can rely on us.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### CTA\n\n**Let\'s build your production.**\n\nThe experience should never feel like a collection of random sections.\n\n---\n\n# FINAL CREATIVE STANDARD\n\nDo not build something that merely satisfies the requirements.\n\nBuild something that makes the client **proud to send the website to an international client.**\n\nWhen a corporate event producer opens the site, they should immediately understand:\n\n**D1 Streams is serious.**\n\nWhen a conference organiser sees it:\n\n**D1 Streams can handle this.**\n\nWhen an artist or festival organiser sees it:\n\n**These people understand live production.**\n\nWhen an international client sees it:\n\n**Location is not a limitation.**\n\nWhen someone reaches the enquiry form:\n\n**I know exactly who I should contact.**\n\nThe final website should feel:\n\n# CINEMATIC.\n\n# TECHNICAL.\n\n# INTERNATIONAL.\n\n# PRECISE.\n\n# PREMIUM.\n\n# TRUSTWORTHY.\n\nDo not over-design it.\n\nDo not make it flashy for the sake of being flashy.\n\nMake it **quietly exceptional**.\n\nEvery typography decision, image, animation, spacing system and interaction should communicate that D1 Streams is a company capable of handling moments that **cannot be repeated.**\n\nBuild the website to a level where the client does not feel like they received a website.\n\nThey should feel like they received a **world-class digital identity for their company.**\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: # D1 STREAMS \342\200\224 WORLD-CLASS INTERNATIONAL WEBSITE\n\nDesign and build a **premium, production-ready website for D1 Streams**, an international live streaming and media production company established in 2021, based in the UK and operating globally.\n\nThis website is being built for a real international-facing client.\n\nThe objective is not simply to make the website \342\200\234look good.\342\200\235\n\nThe objective is to create a digital experience that makes a potential client immediately think:\n\n> **\342\200\234These people know broadcast production. I can trust them with my event.\342\200\235**\n\nThe final website should feel comparable to the digital presence of a serious international broadcast, live-production, creative-technology, or event-production company.\n\nIt must feel **premium, cinematic, technically credible, sophisticated, confident and internationally relevant.**\n\n---\n\n# 01 \342\200\224 OFFICIAL BRAND IDENTITY\n\nCompany:\n\n**D1 STREAMS**\n\nOfficial tagline:\n\n**BROADCAST QUALITY. ANYWHERE. ANYTIME.**\n\nThe official D1 Streams logo has already been created.\n\n## LOGO \342\200\224 CRITICAL REQUIREMENT\n\nUse the **official D1 Streams logo provided with this project**.\n\nDO NOT:\n\n* redesign the logo\n* redraw the symbol\n* modify its geometry\n* change its proportions\n* distort it\n* stretch it\n* rotate it\n* recreate it with another AI-generated logo\n* replace it with a generic streaming icon\n* add unnecessary effects to it\n\nThe logo must remain visually identical to the approved brand identity.\n\nBuild the website\'s visual language around the logo.\n\nThe logo should appear in:\n\n* Desktop navigation\n* Mobile navigation\n* Footer\n* Appropriate brand moments\n* Favicon / browser identity where applicable\n\nGive the logo appropriate clear space.\n\n---\n\n# 02 \342\200\224 BRAND POSITIONING\n\nD1 Streams is a professional live broadcast and production company.\n\nThe company provides:\n\n* Multi-camera live streaming\n* Live switching / vision mixing\n* Professional broadcast audio integration\n* On-site production\n* Technical direction\n* Broadcast graphics\n* Lower thirds\n* Branded overlays\n* Multi-platform streaming\n* Custom RTMP streaming\n* Recording and archiving\n* LED screen integration\n* Hybrid event production\n* Remote production\n* Scalable camera systems\n* Full production crew\n* International production support\n\nD1 Streams can support productions ranging from intimate events to large conferences, concerts, festivals and complex international productions.\n\nThe website must communicate:\n\n**Professional production.\nTechnical excellence.\nReliability.\nGlobal capability.\nBroadcast quality.**\n\n---\n\n# 03 \342\200\224 THE BIG IDEA\n\nThe website should be built around one central idea:\n\n## \342\200\234WE DON\'T JUST STREAM THE EVENT. WE PRODUCE THE BROADCAST.\342\200\235\n\nThis should become one of the strongest pieces of messaging throughout the experience.\n\nD1 Streams should not be positioned as someone who simply presses \342\200\234Go Live.\342\200\235\n\nPosition the company as the technical and creative team responsible for turning a physical event into a professional live broadcast.\n\n---\n\n# 04 \342\200\224 VISUAL ART DIRECTION\n\nCreate a **cinematic editorial broadcast aesthetic**.\n\nThink:\n\n**International broadcast studio \303\227 premium editorial magazine \303\227 live-event production \303\227 technical precision.**\n\nThe website should feel:\n\n* Cinematic\n* Premium\n* Intelligent\n* Precise\n* Technical\n* Confident\n* International\n* Modern\n* Energetic\n* Minimal\n* Timeless\n\nAvoid generic startup aesthetics.\n\nDo NOT make this look like:\n\n* A SaaS website\n* A generic marketing template\n* A cheap event videographer website\n* A wedding photography website\n* A gaming website\n* An AI startup\n* A generic \342\200\234streaming service\342\200\235 landing page\n\nAvoid excessive:\n\n* gradients\n* neon\n* glow effects\n* glassmorphism\n* floating blobs\n* random 3D objects\n* abstract AI graphics\n* oversized rounded cards\n* generic play buttons\n* generic camera illustrations\n* microphone icons\n* Wi-Fi icons\n* film-reel icons\n* unnecessary decorative shapes\n\nPremium should come from:\n\n**Typography + composition + photography + scale + whitespace + contrast + motion.**\n\n---\n\n# 05 \342\200\224 COLOR DIRECTION\n\nUse a sophisticated dark visual foundation.\n\nPrimary palette:\n\n* Deep black\n* Near-black\n* Charcoal\n* Graphite\n* Warm white / off-white\n* Restrained accent derived from the official D1 Streams identity\n\nDo not introduce random colors.\n\nThe brand accent should be used sparingly for:\n\n* CTAs\n* links\n* active states\n* small highlights\n* interactive elements\n* important technical details\n\nThe website should feel premium rather than colorful.\n\n---\n\n# 06 \342\200\224 TYPOGRAPHY\n\nTypography is one of the most important elements of the design.\n\nUse a premium contemporary sans-serif system.\n\nCreate a strong typographic hierarchy:\n\n### DISPLAY\n\nLarge, powerful headlines.\n\n### LABELS\n\nSmall uppercase technical labels.\n\n### BODY\n\nHighly readable and restrained.\n\n### METADATA\n\nCompact technical information.\n\nUse typography to create visual rhythm.\n\nAvoid excessive font weights and unnecessary typefaces.\n\n---\n\n# 07 \342\200\224 HERO\n\nThe hero must immediately communicate the scale and professionalism of D1 Streams.\n\nUse a cinematic, full-screen visual environment.\n\nThe imagery should represent **real professional live production**, such as:\n\n* Multi-camera event coverage\n* Camera operators\n* Broadcast control\n* Vision mixing\n* Stage production\n* Concerts\n* Conferences\n* LED environments\n* Professional crews\n* Live audiences\n\nAvoid generic stock images of people holding cameras.\n\nThe hero should feel like the viewer has stepped inside a professional production.\n\n### HERO COPY\n\nEyebrow:\n\n**UK BASED \302\267 GLOBAL PRODUCTION**\n\nHeadline:\n\n# LIVE EVENTS.\n\n# BUILT FOR BROADCAST.\n\nSupporting copy:\n\n**Professional multi-camera production and live streaming for conferences, concerts, festivals, corporate events, churches and experiences anywhere in the world.**\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\n**PLAN YOUR PRODUCTION \342\206\222**\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\n**EXPLORE CAPABILITIES**\n\nBelow or around the hero, subtly communicate:\n\n**BROADCAST QUALITY. ANYWHERE. ANYTIME.**\n\n---\n\n# 08 \342\200\224 TRUST STRIP\n\nImmediately after the hero, establish technical credibility.\n\nUse a refined horizontal capability strip:\n\n**MULTI-CAMERA**\n\n**LIVE SWITCHING**\n\n**BROADCAST AUDIO**\n\n**LIVE GRAPHICS**\n\n**MULTI-PLATFORM**\n\n**GLOBAL PRODUCTION**\n\nThis should feel like a broadcast specification rather than a generic feature list.\n\n---\n\n# 09 \342\200\224 INTRODUCTION\n\nCreate a strong editorial introduction.\n\nEyebrow:\n\n**D1 STREAMS**\n\nHeadline:\n\n# YOUR EVENT.\n\n# OUR BROADCAST.\n\nBody:\n\nD1 Streams transforms live events into polished, professional broadcasts designed for audiences wherever they are watching.\n\nFrom intimate gatherings to large-scale conferences, concerts and festivals, our production teams combine professional equipment, experienced crew and reliable live workflows to deliver exceptional coverage in real time.\n\nStrong closing statement:\n\n# WE DON\'T JUST STREAM THE EVENT.\n\n# WE PRODUCE THE BROADCAST.\n\nMake this statement visually dominant.\n\n---\n\n# 10 \342\200\224 CAPABILITIES\n\nHeadline:\n\n# EVERYTHING BETWEEN\n\n# THE STAGE AND THE SCREEN.\n\nCreate a premium interactive capabilities experience.\n\nDo not simply create eight identical cards.\n\nUse an editorial layout with large typography, imagery and subtle interactions.\n\nCapabilities:\n\n### MULTI-CAMERA PRODUCTION\n\nProfessional multi-camera coverage designed to capture the event from multiple perspectives.\n\n### LIVE SWITCHING\n\nReal-time vision mixing and camera direction for dynamic broadcast-quality coverage.\n\n### BROADCAST AUDIO\n\nProfessional audio integration designed to deliver clear, balanced sound to the online audience.\n\n### GRAPHICS & OVERLAYS\n\nBranded titles, lower thirds, transitions and live visual systems.\n\n### MULTI-PLATFORM STREAMING\n\nStream simultaneously to YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, Twitch or custom RTMP destinations.\n\n### ON-SITE PRODUCTION\n\nTechnical direction and experienced production crew managing the live workflow.\n\n### LED & HYBRID PRODUCTION\n\nIntegration with LED environments, presentations and hybrid event systems.\n\n### RECORDING & ARCHIVE\n\nReliable local recording and archival so the production can continue beyond the livestream.\n\n---\n\n# 11 \342\200\224 PRODUCTION PROCESS\n\nHeadline:\n\n# FROM BRIEF\n\n# TO BROADCAST.\n\nCreate a sophisticated numbered process.\n\n### 01 \342\200\224 UNDERSTAND\n\nWe understand your event, audience, venue, schedule and production requirements.\n\n### 02 \342\200\224 PLAN\n\nWe design the production workflow, camera configuration, streaming architecture and technical requirements.\n\n### 03 \342\200\224 PRODUCE\n\nOur crew manages the live production, switching, audio, graphics and broadcast workflow.\n\n### 04 \342\200\224 DELIVER\n\nYour broadcast reaches audiences across the platforms that matter.\n\n### 05 \342\200\224 ARCHIVE\n\nWhere required, the production is recorded and preserved for future use.\n\nUse subtle transitions as the user moves through the process.\n\n---\n\n# 12 \342\200\224 EVENTS\n\nHeadline:\n\n# WHATEVER THE EVENT.\n\n# WHEREVER THE AUDIENCE.\n\nShow:\n\n**CONFERENCES & SUMMITS**\n\n**CONCERTS & FESTIVALS**\n\n**CHURCHES & MINISTRIES**\n\n**CORPORATE EVENTS**\n\n**BRAND ACTIVATIONS**\n\n**WEDDINGS & PRIVATE EVENTS**\n\n**SPORTS & TOURNAMENTS**\n\n**PRODUCT LAUNCHES**\n\n**GRADUATIONS**\n\n**CHARITY & FUNDRAISING**\n\n**VIRTUAL & HYBRID EVENTS**\n\nUse large cinematic imagery.\n\nDo not make this look like a generic icon grid.\n\n---\n\n# 13 \342\200\224 GLOBAL CAPABILITY\n\nThis section is essential.\n\nD1 Streams must feel genuinely international.\n\nHeadline:\n\n# ONE PRODUCTION TEAM.\n\n# NO FIXED BOUNDARIES.\n\nCopy:\n\n**Based in the UK and built for productions beyond it, D1 Streams provides scalable live-production workflows wherever the event takes place.**\n\nCreate a visual narrative showing production scale.\n\nExample:\n\n**1 CAMERA \342\206\222 MULTI-CAMERA \342\206\222 FULL BROADCAST PRODUCTION**\n\nCommunicate:\n\n**UK BASED**\n\n**GLOBAL DEPLOYMENT**\n\n**SCALABLE PRODUCTION**\n\nDo not fabricate specific international offices or locations.\n\nDo not create fake global statistics.\n\n---\n\n# 14 \342\200\224 PRODUCTION LEVELS\n\nPresent the service levels elegantly.\n\nDo not make this look like a cheap SaaS pricing table.\n\n### STARTER\n\nFor intimate and smaller events.\n\n1\342\200\2232 cameras\nBasic audio integration\nSingle streaming platform\nRecording\n\n### STANDARD\n\nFor medium events, churches and corporate productions.\n\n3\342\200\2234 cameras\nLive switching\nBroadcast graphics\nUp to 2 platforms\nRecording\n\n### PREMIUM\n\nFor large conferences, concerts and festivals.\n\n4\342\200\2236 cameras\nFull production crew\nAdvanced graphics\nMulti-platform streaming\nLED integration\nRecording & archive\n\n### GLOBAL ELITE\n\nFor major international and complex productions.\n\nCustom production\nMulti-day events\nGlobal crew deployment\nFull broadcast infrastructure\nDedicated production management\n\nImportant message:\n\n**Every production is tailored to the event.**\n\nCTA:\n\n**BUILD MY PRODUCTION \342\206\222**\n\nDo not invent fixed prices unless real prices are supplied.\n\n---\n\n# 15 \342\200\224 WHY D1 STREAMS\n\nHeadline:\n\n# THE DIFFERENCE\n\n# IS IN THE DETAILS.\n\nCreate four sophisticated editorial blocks.\n\n### BROADCAST QUALITY\n\nProfessional workflows designed around the standards of live broadcast production.\n\n### RELIABLE EXECUTION\n\nCareful planning and experienced crews designed to keep the production moving.\n\n### SCALABLE PRODUCTION\n\nFrom a single-camera setup to complex multi-camera environments.\n\n### GLOBAL CAPABILITY\n\nUK-based with the ability to support productions across international locations.\n\n---\n\n# 16 \342\200\224 TECHNICAL CREDIBILITY\n\nHeadline:\n\n# ENGINEERED FOR\n\n# THE LIVE MOMENT.\n\nCreate a visually interesting technical section.\n\nDisplay:\n\n**MULTI-CAMERA**\n\n**LIVE VISION MIXING**\n\n**PROFESSIONAL AUDIO**\n\n**CUSTOM RTMP**\n\n**LOCAL RECORDING**\n\n**LIVE GRAPHICS**\n\n**LED INTEGRATION**\n\n**REMOTE PRODUCTION**\n\nThe presentation should feel closer to a professional broadcast specification sheet than a normal marketing section.\n\n---\n\n# 17 \342\200\224 PRODUCTION IN ACTION\n\nD1 Streams currently does not have an extensive professional photography/video library.\n\nTherefore:\n\nUse carefully selected premium event-production imagery to establish the visual atmosphere and demonstrate the type of production D1 Streams delivers.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo not falsely label stock imagery as D1 Streams client work.\n\nDo not invent project names.\n\nDo not create fake case studies.\n\nBuild the visual system so authentic D1 Streams footage can easily replace these images later.\n\nHeadline:\n\n# BUILT FOR THE MOMENTS\n\n# THAT CANNOT BE REPEATED.\n\n---\n\n# 18 \342\200\224 TESTIMONIALS\n\nCreate the testimonial architecture, but do not invent testimonials.\n\nIf verified client testimonials are not supplied:\n\nEither hide this section or create a clearly reserved structure that can be populated later.\n\nAuthenticity is more important than filling every section.\n\n---\n\n# 19 \342\200\224 FAQ\n\nCreate an elegant accordion FAQ.\n\nQuestions:\n\n* What types of events do you cover?\n* Do you operate outside the UK?\n* How many cameras can you provide?\n* Which platforms can you stream to?\n* Can you stream to custom RTMP destinations?\n* Do you provide on-site production crews?\n* Can you integrate with existing venue audio?\n* Can you integrate LED screens?\n* Can you provide recording?\n* How far in advance should we book?\n* Can you create a custom production package?\n\n---\n\n# 20 \342\200\224 FINAL CTA\n\nCreate a dramatic final section.\n\nHeadline:\n\n# READY WHEN\n\n# THE MOMENT GOES LIVE.\n\nSupporting copy:\n\n**Tell us what you\'re producing, where it\'s happening and what your audience needs. We\'ll build the production around it.**\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\n**PLAN YOUR PRODUCTION \342\206\222**\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\n**WHATSAPP THE TEAM**\n\nThe final CTA should feel like the natural conclusion of the website.\n\n---\n\n# 21 \342\200\224 PRODUCTION ENQUIRY\n\nCreate a premium enquiry experience.\n\nHeadline:\n\n# LET\'S PLAN\n\n# YOUR PRODUCTION.\n\nCollect:\n\n* Event name\n* Event type\n* Event date\n* Event time\n* Venue\n* City / Country\n* Estimated attendance\n* Event duration\n* Number of cameras required\n* Streaming platforms\n* Production requirements\n* Budget range\n* Special requests\n* Name\n* Company / Organisation\n* Email\n* Phone / WhatsApp\n\nMake the form feel simple and premium.\n\nDo not overwhelm the user with unnecessary fields.\n\nConfirmation message:\n\n**Thank you. We\'ve received your production brief and will be in touch with the next steps.**\n\nDo not create fake backend functionality if a backend has not been implemented.\n\n---\n\n# 22 \342\200\224 NAVIGATION\n\nDesktop:\n\nD1 STREAMS logo\n\nCapabilities\nEvents\nHow We Work\nAbout\nFAQ\n\nCTA:\n\n**PLAN YOUR PRODUCTION**\n\nThe navigation should be minimal.\n\nHero navigation can begin transparent/overlayed and transition elegantly when scrolling.\n\nMobile navigation must be exceptionally clean.\n\n---\n\n# 23 \342\200\224 FOOTER\n\nCreate a sophisticated minimal footer.\n\nD1 STREAMS\n\n**Broadcast Quality. Anywhere. Anytime.**\n\nUK BASED \302\267 GLOBAL PRODUCTION\n\nNavigation:\n\nCapabilities\nEvents\nHow We Work\nAbout\nFAQ\nContact\n\nContact:\n\n**+44 7918 916398**\n\n**[dammyondnet@gmail.com](mailto:dammyondnet@gmail.com)**\n\nSocial:\n\n**Instagram \342\200\224 @d1_streams**\n\n**TikTok \342\200\224 @d1_streams**\n\nThen include a very subtle professional development credit:\n\n**A digital experience by NAMACO Technology Nigeria Limited**\n\nThis credit should be small and understated.\n\nIt should NOT compete with the D1 Streams brand.\n\nIf NAMACO has an official website, make the credit link to it.\n\nCopyright:\n\n**\302\251 2026 D1 Streams. All rights reserved.**\n\n---\n\n# 24 \342\200\224 MOTION SYSTEM\n\nMotion should feel cinematic and expensive.\n\nUse:\n\n* smooth reveal animations\n* subtle image scaling\n* elegant text transitions\n* restrained parallax\n* sophisticated hover states\n* navigation transitions\n* subtle horizontal movement\n* smooth scrolling\n* staggered section entrances\n\nAvoid:\n\n* bouncing animations\n* excessive spinning\n* flashy transitions\n* constant movement\n* distracting cursor effects\n* unnecessary 3D\n* animation that harms performance\n\nThe motion should communicate:\n\n**Precision. Control. Confidence.**\n\n---\n\n# 25 \342\200\224 IMAGERY\n\nImage selection is extremely important.\n\nPrioritize images showing:\n\n* Professional broadcast cameras\n* Camera operators\n* Vision control rooms\n* Concert stages\n* Corporate conferences\n* Large audiences\n* LED screens\n* Production crews\n* Live event environments\n* Technical direction\n* Behind-the-scenes production\n\nImages should feel:\n\n**cinematic, authentic, premium and editorial.**\n\nAvoid:\n\n* cheesy stock photos\n* obvious staged photography\n* generic people smiling at cameras\n* low-quality event photographs\n* clich\303\251 \342\200\234social media livestream\342\200\235 images\n\nUse strong cropping and full-bleed compositions.\n\n---\n\n# 26 \342\200\224 RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n\nThe site must be genuinely responsive.\n\nDesign specifically for:\n\n* Large desktop\n* Desktop\n* Tablet\n* Mobile\n\nDo not simply shrink the desktop website.\n\nMobile should feel like a deliberately designed premium experience.\n\nPay special attention to:\n\n* hero typography\n* image cropping\n* navigation\n* CTA placement\n* form usability\n* touch targets\n* section spacing\n* horizontal content\n* performance\n\n---\n\n# 27 \342\200\224 ACCESSIBILITY\n\nMaintain:\n\n* strong color contrast\n* readable typography\n* semantic HTML\n* keyboard navigation\n* visible focus states\n* accessible forms\n* meaningful alt text\n* reduced-motion support\n\nPremium design must never compromise usability.\n\n---\n\n# 28 \342\200\224 SEO\n\nOptimize naturally for relevant searches such as:\n\n* live streaming company UK\n* professional live streaming\n* multi-camera live streaming\n* event live streaming\n* conference live streaming\n* concert live streaming\n* corporate event streaming\n* church live streaming\n* festival live streaming\n* hybrid event production\n* broadcast production\n* live event production\n\nDo not keyword-stuff the website.\n\nThe copy should remain natural and sophisticated.\n\nInclude:\n\n* page title\n* meta description\n* Open Graph metadata\n* structured headings\n* semantic markup\n* proper favicon\n* social sharing image\n* clean URLs\n\n---\n\n# 29 \342\200\224 PERFORMANCE\n\nThe final website must be production-ready.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n* fast loading\n* optimized images\n* responsive images\n* lazy loading\n* minimal unnecessary JavaScript\n* efficient animations\n* excellent Core Web Vitals\n* clean component architecture\n\nDo not sacrifice performance for visual effects.\n\n---\n\n# 30 \342\200\224 CONTENT INTEGRITY\n\nNever fabricate:\n\n* clients\n* testimonials\n* awards\n* partnerships\n* certifications\n* international offices\n* production statistics\n* event statistics\n* equipment ownership\n* projects\n* case studies\n\nIf information is not provided, create a flexible component that can be populated later.\n\nD1 Streams must look established without pretending to have achievements that have not been verified.\n\n---\n\n# 31 \342\200\224 FINAL EXPERIENCE\n\nThe entire website should tell one coherent story:\n\n### HERO\n\n**We produce live broadcasts.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### CAPABILITIES\n\n**This is what we\'re technically capable of.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### PROCESS\n\n**This is how professionally we work.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### EVENTS\n\n**This is where our expertise applies.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### GLOBAL\n\n**This isn\'t limited to one location.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### PRODUCTION LEVELS\n\n**We can scale around your event.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### TRUST\n\n**Here is why you can rely on us.**\n\n\342\206\223\n\n### CTA\n\n**Let\'s build your production.**\n\nThe experience should never feel like a collection of random sections.\n\n---\n\n# FINAL CREATIVE STANDARD\n\nDo not build something that merely satisfies the requirements.\n\nBuild something that makes the client **proud to send the website to an international client.**\n\nWhen a corporate event producer opens the site, they should immediately understand:\n\n**D1 Streams is serious.**\n\nWhen a conference organiser sees it:\n\n**D1 Streams can handle this.**\n\nWhen an artist or festival organiser sees it:\n\n**These people understand live production.**\n\nWhen an international client sees it:\n\n**Location is not a limitation.**\n\nWhen someone reaches the enquiry form:\n\n**I know exactly who I should contact.**\n\nThe final website should feel:\n\n# CINEMATIC.\n\n# TECHNICAL.\n\n# INTERNATIONAL.\n\n# PRECISE.\n\n# PREMIUM.\n\n# TRUSTWORTHY.\n\nDo not over-design it.\n\nDo not make it flashy for the sake of being flashy.\n\nMake it **quietly exceptional**.\n\nEvery typography decision, image, animation, spacing system and interaction should communicate that D1 Streams is a company capable of handling moments that **cannot be repeated.**\n\nBuild the website to a level where the client does not feel like they received a website.\n\nThey should feel like they received a **world-class digital identity for their company.**\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
  }
}
