  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Logo Restrictions**\n\nI\'ve just reviewed the logo requirements, specifically section 01. It\'s clear: the D1 Streams logo is non-negotiable. I need to strictly adhere to the provided version, with no modifications whatsoever. I am to leave the design completely untouched.\n\n\n**Constructing Logo Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focused on the technical implementation. The goal is a pixel-perfect SVG component for the D1 STREAMS logo. \"D1\" will use bold geometric block typography with a red/amber broadcast indicator or metallic red accent. \"STREAMS\" uses clean uppercase sans-serif text. I\'m building `Logo.tsx` for optimal rendering on dark backgrounds. I\'m also ensuring export capabilities for SVG images at any scale.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Principles**\n\nI\'m now establishing the visual identity guidelines. I\'m leaning toward a dark, sophisticated palette: deep blacks, charcoals, and graphite, softened with a warm white. Broadcast Crimson will be the brand accent, used for live indicators. For typography, I am looking at clean, contemporary sans-serif fonts like Inter or Plus Jakarta Sans for a high-contrast display. I\'m focusing on uppercase technical labels with tracking. My next steps are structuring sections for the prompt: header/navigation and hero sections.\n\n\n**Formulating Landing Page**\n\nI\'m now outlining the landing page content. I\'ve defined the primary and secondary CTAs, and a tagline. I\'m visualizing a live broadcast feed simulator element, with interactive camera switcher, tally lights, signal stats, and audio meters. I\'ve also planned a \"Trust Strip\" and introduction section with headline, eyebrow, body text, and a dominant statement. The aim is a strong visual and technical presentation. I\'m now structuring the capabilities section.\n\n\n**Structuring Capability Display**\n\nI\'ve just structured the core capabilities and production process into specific visual sections. I\'m focusing on features such as multi-camera production, and am organizing event coverage into a dynamic cinematic image grid. I am thinking of a global capability headline \"ONE PRODUCTION TEAM. NO FIXED BOUNDARIES.\"\n\n\n**Expanding Production Scope**\n\nI\'m now detailing D1 Streams\' scalability. I am visualizing a production scale progression: \"1 CAMERA \342\206\222 MULTI-CAMERA \342\206\222 FULL BROADCAST PRODUCTION.\" I\'m also planning badges: \"UK BASED,\" \"GLOBAL DEPLOYMENT,\" and \"SCALABLE PRODUCTION.\" An interactive world map simulator is next, showcasing global deployment logistics. I\'ve also defined service tiers: STARTER, STANDARD, PREMIUM, and GLOBAL ELITE, each with specific features. I\'m communicating that every production is tailored.\n\n\n**Defining Production Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Why D1 Streams\" section, focusing on broadcast quality, reliable execution, scalable production, and global capabilities, structuring these ideas into distinct editorial blocks. Next, I am thinking of a technical credibility section with an interactive spec sheet, including switcher diagrams, audio processing, and camera specs. Then, I am going to make a \"Production in Action\" section, and am planning a cinematic gallery. I\'m also preparing a dedicated section for verified client testimonials. I am ready to build an interactive FAQ.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
