  planner_response {
    response: "I have designed and built the world-class international website for **D1 STREAMS**.\n\n### **Design & Visual Art Direction**\n- **Cinematic Dark Foundation**: Structured around a deep obsidian canvas (`#0A0A0B`) with charcoal grid accents (`#121214`) and warm off-white typography (`#F4F4F6`).\n- **Official Brand Identity**: Integrated the official **D1 STREAMS** logo geometry and typography across the desktop navigation, mobile drawer, and footer, paired with the official tagline: ***BROADCAST QUALITY. ANYWHERE. ANYTIME.***\n- **Typographic Hierarchy**: Paired *Syne* for display headlines with *Plus Jakarta Sans* for body copy and *JetBrains Mono* for technical telemetry labels.\n- **Restrained Signal Accent**: Used broadcast crimson (`#E50914`) exclusively for live tally indicators, CTAs, signal paths, and active state highlights.\n\n---\n\n### **Core Experience & Functional Scope**\n1. **Hero Studio Control Room**: Full-screen cinematic environment with an interactive multi-camera vision switcher simulator (CAM 1\342\200\2234), audio VU meters (-14.2 LUFS), lower-third graphics preview, and primary CTAs (*PLAN YOUR PRODUCTION \342\206\222* & *EXPLORE CAPABILITIES*).\n2. **Specification Trust Strip**: Horizontal specification bar highlighting *Multi-Camera, Live Switching, Broadcast Audio, Live Graphics, Multi-Platform, Global Production*.\n3. **Editorial Introduction & Big Idea**: Highlights the central philosophy: ***\"WE DON\'T JUST STREAM THE EVENT. WE PRODUCE THE BROADCAST.\"***\n4. **Interactive Capabilities Grid**: Deep technical breakdown across all 8 core services with equipment lists and a modal technical inspector.\n5. **Process Timeline (01 to 05)**: From Brief to Broadcast (*Understand, Plan, Produce, Deliver, Archive*) with deliverable tracking.\n6. **Sector Showcases**: Comprehensive coverage across 11 event types (Conferences, Concerts, Churches, Corporate, Brand Activations, Weddings, Sports, Product Launches, Graduations, Charity, Virtual/Hybrid).\n7. **Global Capability**: Showcases UK base dispatch capabilities and production scale progression (*1 Camera \342\206\222 Multi-Camera \342\206\222 Full Broadcast Production*).\n8. **Bespoke Service Levels & Configurator**: STARTER, STANDARD, PREMIUM, and GLOBAL ELITE tiers alongside an interactive **Production Configurator** drawer.\n9. **Technical Specification Sheet**: Full broadcast engineering breakdown (*12G-SDI, Dante Audio, EBU R128, SRT/RTMP, Apple ProRes ISO Archives*).\n10. **Atmospheric Production Gallery**: High-definition control room, camera rig, and stage production imagery.\n11. **Authenticity & Integrity**: Reserved client confidentiality architecture for NDA-protected productions.\n12. **Complete Accordion FAQ**: All 11 questions answered with broadcast engineer precision.\n13. **Production Briefing Enquiry Form**: Interactive form collecting event details, camera setups, platforms, and budget ranges with instant summary reference generation.\n14. **Direct Contact & Footer**: Direct WhatsApp link (`+44 7918 916398`), email (`dammyondnet@gmail.com`), Instagram/TikTok handles (`@d1_streams`), and developer credit for NAMACO Technology Nigeria Limited."
    thinking: "**Verifying Compliance Details**\n\nI\'ve successfully compiled the applet. Now, I\'m meticulously reviewing the prompt\'s guidelines and requirements to guarantee full adherence. Specifically, I am ensuring all details are accurate. I\'m especially focusing on the company name, tagline, and the critical logo requirement; paying close attention to the `Logo.tsx` specification for the red signal tally dot.\n\n\n**Defining the Production Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the brand positioning and visual language. The big idea will anchor the introduction, emphasizing broadcast production. I\'ve chosen the color palette, typography, and Hero section components, including the tagline and a compelling studio switcher simulator. A trust strip and interactive capabilities section are also planned, with a production process section to follow.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have designed and built the world-class international website for **D1 STREAMS**.\n\n### **Design & Visual Art Direction**\n- **Cinematic Dark Foundation**: Structured around a deep obsidian canvas (`#0A0A0B`) with charcoal grid accents (`#121214`) and warm off-white typography (`#F4F4F6`).\n- **Official Brand Identity**: Integrated the official **D1 STREAMS** logo geometry and typography across the desktop navigation, mobile drawer, and footer, paired with the official tagline: ***BROADCAST QUALITY. ANYWHERE. ANYTIME.***\n- **Typographic Hierarchy**: Paired *Syne* for display headlines with *Plus Jakarta Sans* for body copy and *JetBrains Mono* for technical telemetry labels.\n- **Restrained Signal Accent**: Used broadcast crimson (`#E50914`) exclusively for live tally indicators, CTAs, signal paths, and active state highlights.\n\n---\n\n### **Core Experience & Functional Scope**\n1. **Hero Studio Control Room**: Full-screen cinematic environment with an interactive multi-camera vision switcher simulator (CAM 1\342\200\2234), audio VU meters (-14.2 LUFS), lower-third graphics preview, and primary CTAs (*PLAN YOUR PRODUCTION \342\206\222* & *EXPLORE CAPABILITIES*).\n2. **Specification Trust Strip**: Horizontal specification bar highlighting *Multi-Camera, Live Switching, Broadcast Audio, Live Graphics, Multi-Platform, Global Production*.\n3. **Editorial Introduction & Big Idea**: Highlights the central philosophy: ***\"WE DON\'T JUST STREAM THE EVENT. WE PRODUCE THE BROADCAST.\"***\n4. **Interactive Capabilities Grid**: Deep technical breakdown across all 8 core services with equipment lists and a modal technical inspector.\n5. **Process Timeline (01 to 05)**: From Brief to Broadcast (*Understand, Plan, Produce, Deliver, Archive*) with deliverable tracking.\n6. **Sector Showcases**: Comprehensive coverage across 11 event types (Conferences, Concerts, Churches, Corporate, Brand Activations, Weddings, Sports, Product Launches, Graduations, Charity, Virtual/Hybrid).\n7. **Global Capability**: Showcases UK base dispatch capabilities and production scale progression (*1 Camera \342\206\222 Multi-Camera \342\206\222 Full Broadcast Production*).\n8. **Bespoke Service Levels & Configurator**: STARTER, STANDARD, PREMIUM, and GLOBAL ELITE tiers alongside an interactive **Production Configurator** drawer.\n9. **Technical Specification Sheet**: Full broadcast engineering breakdown (*12G-SDI, Dante Audio, EBU R128, SRT/RTMP, Apple ProRes ISO Archives*).\n10. **Atmospheric Production Gallery**: High-definition control room, camera rig, and stage production imagery.\n11. **Authenticity & Integrity**: Reserved client confidentiality architecture for NDA-protected productions.\n12. **Complete Accordion FAQ**: All 11 questions answered with broadcast engineer precision.\n13. **Production Briefing Enquiry Form**: Interactive form collecting event details, camera setups, platforms, and budget ranges with instant summary reference generation.\n14. **Direct Contact & Footer**: Direct WhatsApp link (`+44 7918 916398`), email (`dammyondnet@gmail.com`), Instagram/TikTok handles (`@d1_streams`), and developer credit for NAMACO Technology Nigeria Limited."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 272808299
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
