steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1788743711
      nanos: 41506116
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "# FINAL VISUAL DIRECTION \342\200\224 IMPORTANT\n\nThese requirements are mandatory and should guide the entire website.\n\n## 1. BACKGROUND \342\200\224 CINEMATIC BROADCAST ATMOSPHERE\n\nThe website must NOT use a basic flat black background throughout.\n\nCreate a sophisticated, cinematic background system inspired by **professional live broadcast production**.\n\nThe visual atmosphere should feel like:\n\n**premium broadcast studio + cinematic event production + international media company.**\n\nUse a combination of:\n\n* Deep black\n* Near-black charcoal\n* Graphite\n* Very subtle tonal variations\n* High-quality cinematic event-production photography\n* Darkened production environments\n* Subtle film grain\n* Very restrained texture\n* Natural shadows\n* Atmospheric depth\n* Carefully controlled contrast\n\nUse cinematic photography/video in selected sections showing things such as:\n\n* Professional broadcast cameras\n* Camera operators\n* Large concert stages\n* Corporate conferences\n* LED walls\n* Production control rooms\n* Vision mixing\n* Technical crews\n* Live audiences\n* Behind-the-scenes broadcast environments\n\nImages should feel **real, premium and cinematic**, not like obvious generic stock photography.\n\nUse full-bleed imagery in important sections where appropriate.\n\nDark overlays may be applied over imagery so typography remains highly readable.\n\n### IMPORTANT\n\nDo NOT use:\n\n* Neon backgrounds\n* Cyberpunk visuals\n* Purple/blue AI gradients\n* Glowing network lines\n* Futuristic holograms\n* Floating blobs\n* Generic 3D objects\n* Abstract AI graphics\n* Giant world-map graphics\n* Generic streaming illustrations\n* Excessive glassmorphism\n* Excessive glow effects\n\nThe background should communicate:\n\n**PRODUCTION. SCALE. PRECISION. EXPERIENCE.**\n\nnot \342\200\234AI technology.\342\200\235\n\nCreate visual depth through **photography, lighting, texture, contrast and composition**, not excessive effects.\n\n---\n\n# 2. TYPOGRAPHY \342\200\224 COOL, DISTINCTIVE & PREMIUM\n\nTypography must be one of the strongest parts of the website.\n\nDo NOT use boring default typography.\n\nSelect a **high-end contemporary typeface system** suitable for an international broadcast and media-production company.\n\nThe typography should feel:\n\n**Cool.\nModern.\nEditorial.\nConfident.\nPremium.\nTechnical.\nInternational.**\n\nUse a strong display typeface for major headlines and a highly readable supporting typeface for body copy and interface elements.\n\nThe headline typography should have personality.\n\nLarge headlines should feel like the typography of a premium international media company or creative studio.\n\nUse:\n\n* Large editorial headlines\n* Tight but readable typography\n* Strong scale contrast\n* Small uppercase technical labels\n* Elegant metadata\n* Clean navigation\n* Refined CTA typography\n\nThe typography should create a feeling of **confidence and authority**.\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Generic system fonts\n* Overused startup typography\n* Cartoonish fonts\n* Futuristic sci-fi fonts\n* Excessively geometric fonts\n* Decorative fonts that reduce readability\n\nDo not use too many fonts.\n\nUse a carefully controlled typography system with a maximum of two complementary typefaces.\n\nThe final typography should look **expensive without trying too hard.**\n\n---\n\n# 3. NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED \342\200\224 FOOTER CREDIT\n\nThe website was designed and engineered by:\n\n**NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED**\n\nInclude this company name discreetly in the website footer.\n\nUse the exact text:\n\n**Designed & engineered by NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED**\n\n### VERY IMPORTANT:\n\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED must appear as **plain text only**.\n\nDO NOT:\n\n* Add a URL\n* Add a hyperlink\n* Make the name clickable\n* Add a button\n* Add a separate NAMACO section\n* Add a NAMACO logo\n* Add social links\n* Turn it into a promotional banner\n* Make it visually compete with D1 Streams\n\nIt should be a small, elegant production/design credit at the bottom of the footer.\n\nD1 Streams remains the primary and dominant brand.\n\nThe footer hierarchy should clearly communicate:\n\n**D1 STREAMS**\n\nBroadcast Quality. Anywhere. Anytime.\n\n...\n\n**Designed & engineered by NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED**\n\nThe NAMACO credit should feel like a discreet professional studio credit at the end of a premium project.\n\n---\n\n# 4. OVERALL VISUAL RESULT\n\nThe combination of:\n\n**Cinematic backgrounds\n\n* distinctive typography\n* premium photography\n* deep contrast\n* restrained motion\n* generous spacing\n* precise layout**\n\nshould create a website that feels like the digital home of a **serious international broadcast production company**.\n\nThe website should make the client proud to show it to:\n\n* International corporations\n* Conference organisers\n* Global churches\n* Event production companies\n* Artists\n* Festivals\n* Brands\n* Government organisations\n* NGOs\n* High-profile private clients\n\nThe final impression should be:\n\n**\342\200\234These people know what they are doing.\342\200\235**\n\nNot:\n\n**\342\200\234This is a nice streaming website.\342\200\235**\n\nBuild something that feels **cinematic, technically credible, sophisticated and internationally competitive.**"
    items {
      text: "# FINAL VISUAL DIRECTION \342\200\224 IMPORTANT\n\nThese requirements are mandatory and should guide the entire website.\n\n## 1. BACKGROUND \342\200\224 CINEMATIC BROADCAST ATMOSPHERE\n\nThe website must NOT use a basic flat black background throughout.\n\nCreate a sophisticated, cinematic background system inspired by **professional live broadcast production**.\n\nThe visual atmosphere should feel like:\n\n**premium broadcast studio + cinematic event production + international media company.**\n\nUse a combination of:\n\n* Deep black\n* Near-black charcoal\n* Graphite\n* Very subtle tonal variations\n* High-quality cinematic event-production photography\n* Darkened production environments\n* Subtle film grain\n* Very restrained texture\n* Natural shadows\n* Atmospheric depth\n* Carefully controlled contrast\n\nUse cinematic photography/video in selected sections showing things such as:\n\n* Professional broadcast cameras\n* Camera operators\n* Large concert stages\n* Corporate conferences\n* LED walls\n* Production control rooms\n* Vision mixing\n* Technical crews\n* Live audiences\n* Behind-the-scenes broadcast environments\n\nImages should feel **real, premium and cinematic**, not like obvious generic stock photography.\n\nUse full-bleed imagery in important sections where appropriate.\n\nDark overlays may be applied over imagery so typography remains highly readable.\n\n### IMPORTANT\n\nDo NOT use:\n\n* Neon backgrounds\n* Cyberpunk visuals\n* Purple/blue AI gradients\n* Glowing network lines\n* Futuristic holograms\n* Floating blobs\n* Generic 3D objects\n* Abstract AI graphics\n* Giant world-map graphics\n* Generic streaming illustrations\n* Excessive glassmorphism\n* Excessive glow effects\n\nThe background should communicate:\n\n**PRODUCTION. SCALE. PRECISION. EXPERIENCE.**\n\nnot \342\200\234AI technology.\342\200\235\n\nCreate visual depth through **photography, lighting, texture, contrast and composition**, not excessive effects.\n\n---\n\n# 2. TYPOGRAPHY \342\200\224 COOL, DISTINCTIVE & PREMIUM\n\nTypography must be one of the strongest parts of the website.\n\nDo NOT use boring default typography.\n\nSelect a **high-end contemporary typeface system** suitable for an international broadcast and media-production company.\n\nThe typography should feel:\n\n**Cool.\nModern.\nEditorial.\nConfident.\nPremium.\nTechnical.\nInternational.**\n\nUse a strong display typeface for major headlines and a highly readable supporting typeface for body copy and interface elements.\n\nThe headline typography should have personality.\n\nLarge headlines should feel like the typography of a premium international media company or creative studio.\n\nUse:\n\n* Large editorial headlines\n* Tight but readable typography\n* Strong scale contrast\n* Small uppercase technical labels\n* Elegant metadata\n* Clean navigation\n* Refined CTA typography\n\nThe typography should create a feeling of **confidence and authority**.\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Generic system fonts\n* Overused startup typography\n* Cartoonish fonts\n* Futuristic sci-fi fonts\n* Excessively geometric fonts\n* Decorative fonts that reduce readability\n\nDo not use too many fonts.\n\nUse a carefully controlled typography system with a maximum of two complementary typefaces.\n\nThe final typography should look **expensive without trying too hard.**\n\n---\n\n# 3. NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED \342\200\224 FOOTER CREDIT\n\nThe website was designed and engineered by:\n\n**NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED**\n\nInclude this company name discreetly in the website footer.\n\nUse the exact text:\n\n**Designed & engineered by NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED**\n\n### VERY IMPORTANT:\n\nNAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED must appear as **plain text only**.\n\nDO NOT:\n\n* Add a URL\n* Add a hyperlink\n* Make the name clickable\n* Add a button\n* Add a separate NAMACO section\n* Add a NAMACO logo\n* Add social links\n* Turn it into a promotional banner\n* Make it visually compete with D1 Streams\n\nIt should be a small, elegant production/design credit at the bottom of the footer.\n\nD1 Streams remains the primary and dominant brand.\n\nThe footer hierarchy should clearly communicate:\n\n**D1 STREAMS**\n\nBroadcast Quality. Anywhere. Anytime.\n\n...\n\n**Designed & engineered by NAMACO TECHNOLOGY NIGERIA LIMITED**\n\nThe NAMACO credit should feel like a discreet professional studio credit at the end of a premium project.\n\n---\n\n# 4. OVERALL VISUAL RESULT\n\nThe combination of:\n\n**Cinematic backgrounds\n\n* distinctive typography\n* premium photography\n* deep contrast\n* restrained motion\n* generous spacing\n* precise layout**\n\nshould create a website that feels like the digital home of a **serious international broadcast production company**.\n\nThe website should make the client proud to show it to:\n\n* International corporations\n* Conference organisers\n* Global churches\n* Event production companies\n* Artists\n* Festivals\n* Brands\n* Government organisations\n* NGOs\n* High-profile private clients\n\nThe final impression should be:\n\n**\342\200\234These people know what they are doing.\342\200\235**\n\nNot:\n\n**\342\200\234This is a nice streaming website.\342\200\235**\n\nBuild something that feels **cinematic, technically credible, sophisticated and internationally competitive.**"
