  planner_response {
    response: "Based on a precise audit of the codebase (`/src/components/ProductionEnquirySection.tsx`), here is the exact message-delivery flow for the **Production Enquiry** form:\n\n---\n\n### 1. What happens when a visitor submits the form?\nWhen the form is submitted, the React submit handler (`handleSubmit`) executes:\n```ts\nconst handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  setSubmitted(true);\n};\n```\nThis updates local React state (`submitted = true`), causing the UI to transition immediately from the form inputs to an on-screen confirmation card (`\"BRIEF RECEIVED\"`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Is the submission stored anywhere?\n**No.** The submitted data (`formData`) exists exclusively in the browser\'s temporary React component state (`useState`). It is not persisted in `localStorage`, `session-[#0066FF]`, or any external database. If the browser tab is refreshed or closed, the entered brief data is cleared.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Is an email notification sent?\n**No.** Submitting the form does not trigger an outbound network request or automated email dispatch.\n\n---\n\n### 4. If yes, which email address receives it?\n**None.** Because no backend or transactional email service is wired to the form submission event, no email is sent automatically. \n\n*(Note: The page provides direct `mailto:dammyondnet@gmail.com` links above the form and in the footer so visitors can manually click to email `dammyondnet@gmail.com` directly from their email app).*\n\n---\n\n### 5. What email service/backend is being used?\n**None.** The application currently runs as a client-side Single Page Application (SPA). There is no active email delivery provider (such as Resend, SendGrid, EmailJS, Formspree, or Nodemailer) connected to the form submission handler.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Does the visitor receive a confirmation?\n* **On-Screen Confirmation:** **Yes.** The visitor sees an immediate, visual on-screen confirmation modal with the headline **`BRIEF RECEIVED`**. It displays a formatted summary of their inputs and includes a **`COPY BRIEF`** button so they can copy the technical specification text to their clipboard.\n* **Email Confirmation:** **No.** No automated confirmation email is sent to the visitor\'s email address.\n\n---\n\n### 7. What is missing to deliver submissions automatically?\nTo make the form automatically send emails or store messages, one of the following mechanisms needs to be implemented:\n\n1. **Third-Party Form Gateway** *(Fastest setup)*:\n   - Point the form POST action or `fetch()` call to a form handling service like **Formspree**, **Web3Forms**, or **Formbold** linked to `dammyondnet@gmail.com`.\n\n2. **Server API Route & Email SDK**:\n   - Create an Express backend endpoint (e.g. `/api/enquiry`) in a server entry point.\n   - Integrate an email API service (such as **Resend**, **SendGrid**, or **Postmark**) using an API key to dispatch an email to `dammyondnet@gmail.com` and a confirmation receipt to the visitor.\n\n3. **Cloud Database Storage**:\n   - Integrate **Firebase Firestore** to record all submitted production briefs in a persistent collection for admin review."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Form Submission**\n\nI\'ve started to break down the user form submission process within `ProductionEnquirySection.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining the initial actions triggered when a visitor submits the form. The `handleSubmit` function is the entry point, and it calls `e.preventDefault()`, immediately followed by a state update using `setSubmitted(true)`.\n\n\n**Reviewing Client-Side Logic**\n\nI\'ve determined that the form submission triggers a UI update to a success screen with a \"COPY BRIEF\" option. This copies the brief summary to the user\'s clipboard. However, the data isn\'t persisted anywhere on the backend; it\'s purely client-side state. I\'ve confirmed that no email notifications are currently automated upon submission.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Based on a precise audit of the codebase (`/src/components/ProductionEnquirySection.tsx`), here is the exact message-delivery flow for the **Production Enquiry** form:\n\n---\n\n### 1. What happens when a visitor submits the form?\nWhen the form is submitted, the React submit handler (`handleSubmit`) executes:\n```ts\nconst handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {\n  e.preventDefault();\n  setSubmitted(true);\n};\n```\nThis updates local React state (`submitted = true`), causing the UI to transition immediately from the form inputs to an on-screen confirmation card (`\"BRIEF RECEIVED\"`).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Is the submission stored anywhere?\n**No.** The submitted data (`formData`) exists exclusively in the browser\'s temporary React component state (`useState`). It is not persisted in `localStorage`, `session-[#0066FF]`, or any external database. If the browser tab is refreshed or closed, the entered brief data is cleared.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Is an email notification sent?\n**No.** Submitting the form does not trigger an outbound network request or automated email dispatch.\n\n---\n\n### 4. If yes, which email address receives it?\n**None.** Because no backend or transactional email service is wired to the form submission event, no email is sent automatically. \n\n*(Note: The page provides direct `mailto:dammyondnet@gmail.com` links above the form and in the footer so visitors can manually click to email `dammyondnet@gmail.com` directly from their email app).*\n\n---\n\n### 5. What email service/backend is being used?\n**None.** The application currently runs as a client-side Single Page Application (SPA). There is no active email delivery provider (such as Resend, SendGrid, EmailJS, Formspree, or Nodemailer) connected to the form submission handler.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Does the visitor receive a confirmation?\n* **On-Screen Confirmation:** **Yes.** The visitor sees an immediate, visual on-screen confirmation modal with the headline **`BRIEF RECEIVED`**. It displays a formatted summary of their inputs and includes a **`COPY BRIEF`** button so they can copy the technical specification text to their clipboard.\n* **Email Confirmation:** **No.** No automated confirmation email is sent to the visitor\'s email address.\n\n---\n\n### 7. What is missing to deliver submissions automatically?\nTo make the form automatically send emails or store messages, one of the following mechanisms needs to be implemented:\n\n1. **Third-Party Form Gateway** *(Fastest setup)*:\n   - Point the form POST action or `fetch()` call to a form handling service like **Formspree**, **Web3Forms**, or **Formbold** linked to `dammyondnet@gmail.com`.\n\n2. **Server API Route & Email SDK**:\n   - Create an Express backend endpoint (e.g. `/api/enquiry`) in a server entry point.\n   - Integrate an email API service (such as **Resend**, **SendGrid**, or **Postmark**) using an API key to dispatch an email to `dammyondnet@gmail.com` and a confirmation receipt to the visitor.\n\n3. **Cloud Database Storage**:\n   - Integrate **Firebase Firestore** to record all submitted production briefs in a persistent collection for admin review."
