  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Visual Aesthete**\n\nI\'m currently focused on visually transforming D1 Streams. The goal is a luxurious, editorial, cinematic feel for an international media production aesthetic. I am working on the tonal palette and section rhythm. I\'m exploring a dark, light, charcoal, stone sequence to structure visual flow.\n\n\n**Analyzing Visual Flows**\n\nI am now closely analyzing the visual flows. I\'m focusing on the hero section: cinematic dark production environment. I\'m thinking how to make sure the trust strip provides a smooth transition with muted graphite. The goal is to craft a rich tonal range. I am considering light stone and charcoal shades, and exploring borders with a champagne/silver feel.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Tones**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the specific color palette. The goal is a consistent and high-end feel throughout. I\'ve defined deep graphite for global capability, a refined light stone or charcoal for production levels, and rich deep slate for the \"Why D1 Streams\" section. I\'m focusing on high-contrast dark studio consoles for technical credibility and cinematic photography for production in action, and am using a warm light stone and silver for recent work display.\n\n\n**Integrating Color Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating refined color details. I am focusing on subtle champagne and silver accents to complement the deep slate. The goal is to use a sophisticated royal cobalt/slate indigo (#2563EB or #1D4ED8). I am mindful to use warm white and soft silver sparingly. I\'m actively avoiding neon blues and glaring cyberpunk tones and ensuring camera highlights shine through photography overlays.\n\n\n"
