    session_summary: "1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Visual Refinement (Luxurious, Not Too Dark):** The user requested a shift from a \"black/dark\" aesthetic to a \"luxurious, international media-production\" aesthetic.\n  - **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION (Not started on the actual code changes yet).\n  - **Details:** Transition from near-black backgrounds to a sophisticated palette (charcoal, graphite, gunmetal, soft stone, warm off-white). Create visual rhythm by alternating light and dark sections. Reduce heavy black overlays on photography to allow highlights and detail to show.\n- **Form Delivery Implementation:** The user previously asked where form submissions go. It was confirmed that the form is client-side only and does not deliver submissions. No further action was requested to build a backend, but the user is aware of the current state.\n  - **Status:** NOT STARTED.\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- **Preferences:**\n  - \"Cinematic broadcast photography,\" \"Syne\" headlines, \"Plus Jakarta Sans\" body, \"JetBrains Mono\" technical labels.\n  - \"No fake testimonials, no fake logos, no fabricated statistics.\"\n  - \"The goal is to make D1 Streams look credible because of real experience, not because of invented testimonials.\"\n- **Aesthetic Goal:** \"Cinematic + Luxurious + Editorial + Professional + Technical.\"\n- **Palette/Tone:** Avoid \"generic dark-mode technology startup.\" Use a rhythm of \"LIGHT \342\206\222 SHADOW \342\206\222 IMAGE \342\206\222 TYPOGRAPHY \342\206\222 SPACE \342\206\222 LIGHT.\"\n- **Constraint:** Do not introduce neon blue, purple gradients, cyberpunk colors, or excessive gold. Keep the identity sophisticated and contemporary.\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- **Visual Updates (Cinematic):** Updated `Hero`, `Capabilities`, `GlobalCapability`, `ProductionInAction`, and `FinalCTA` to feature prominent, cinematic broadcast photography with optimized gradients and overlays.\n- **Functional Fixes:**\n  - Implemented semantic `mailto:`, `tel:`, and `wa.me` links across the site (Footer, Enquiry Section, Final CTA, Navbar) to ensure contact methods work.\n  - Fixed `ReferenceError: Mail is not defined` in `FinalCTA.tsx` by correcting the `lucide-react` import.\n- **Content Updates:** Replaced all fake testimonials with a \"Recent Production Work\" section featuring:\n  - RCCG Jesus Palace\n  - RCCG Zone of Resurrection\n  - RCCG Peace Arena\n- **Discovery:** Mapped out the form submission logic in `ProductionEnquirySection.tsx`, confirming it is purely client-side and does not send emails or store data.\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture:** The site is a React SPA. Navigation and layout are controlled in `App.tsx`.\n- **Component Structure:**\n  - `Hero.tsx`: Cinematic entry point.\n  - `Testimonials.tsx` (now \"Recent Production Work\"): Credibility section.\n  - `ProductionEnquirySection.tsx`: Client-side form only.\n  - `FinalCTA.tsx`: Final conversion point with contact links.\n- **Dependencies:** Uses `lucide-react` for icons and `motion/react` for animations.\n- **Constraint:** The current dark theme is applied via Tailwind classes (e.g., `bg-[#070709]`, `bg-[#0A0A0B]`). The next phase requires systematic replacement of these background classes to create the requested light/dark rhythm.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files:**\n  - `/src/components/Hero.tsx`: Updated background image and gradient scrims for visibility.\n  - `/src/components/Capabilities.tsx`: Updated background and imagery.\n  - `/src/components/GlobalCapability.tsx`: Updated background and imagery.\n  - `/src/components/FinalCTA.tsx`: Added contact links and fixed `Mail` icon import.\n  - `/src/components/Footer.tsx`: Added functional contact links and social icons.\n  - `/src/components/ProductionEnquirySection.tsx`: Added contact links and updated layout.\n  - `/src/components/Testimonials.tsx`: Replaced testimonials with \"Recent Production Work.\"\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Contains the main layout structure and section order.\n  - `/package.json`: Checked dependencies.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Immediate Task:** Begin the visual refinement to move away from the \"all-black\" aesthetic.\n- **Next Steps:**\n  1. Open `/src/App.tsx` to review the section order.\n  2. Systematically edit section components (e.g., `Introduction.tsx`, `Capabilities.tsx`, `ProductionProcess.tsx`, `EventsCovered.tsx`, `WhyD1Streams.tsx`, `TechnicalCredibility.tsx`, `FAQSection.tsx`) to implement the light/dark rhythm.\n  3. Replace `bg-[#0A0A0B]` or similar dark backgrounds with lighter, sophisticated tones (e.g., `bg-zinc-100`, `bg-stone-50`, or similar) for alternating sections.\n  4. Ensure text contrast is maintained (e.g., switch `text-white` to `text-zinc-900` on light backgrounds).\n  5. Refine photography overlays to be lighter and more cinematic.\n- **User Quote:** \"The goal is: CINEMATIC + LUXURIOUS + EDITORIAL + PROFESSIONAL + TECHNICAL... Not: BLACK + DARK + BLACK + DARK.\""
