  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Entertainment Value**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously examining requirement three, specifically focusing on the entertainment and production aspects of D1 Streams. The core idea is that YouTube needs to be more than a simple link. I\'m exploring how to implement a subtle CTA, perhaps \"WATCH THE PRODUCTION,\" with supporting copy that emphasizes the live-production nature of the company.\n\n\n**Developing Channel Integration**\n\nI\'m now focused on the visual integration of the YouTube presence. The goal is a seamless blend of live events, production, broadcast, and content. Rather than just a row of social icons, it should feel like a cohesive, cinematic experience. I\'m exploring the best way to do this in code, either as a standalone component like `YouTubeShowcase.tsx` or `BroadcastMedia.tsx`, or integrate into the existing component. This section will include a titled banner and conceptual flow badge, such as **BROADCAST & MEDIA CHANNEL**.\n\n\n**Visualizing The Integration**\n\nI\'m now concretely envisioning the visual elements.  The plan is to showcase a \"LIVE EVENTS \342\206\222 PRODUCTION \342\206\222 BROADCAST \342\206\222 CONTENT\" tagline and a \"WATCH THE PRODUCTION\" badge. I\'m imagining visual cards featuring a broadcast control room, live switching, and festival feeds. The call to action will be a \"WATCH ON YOUTUBE \342\206\222\" button linking to the channel.  I\'m also preparing a card with links to all the official social handles, including YouTube, Instagram, TikTok, WhatsApp, email, and phone, to ensure a comprehensive integration.\n\n\n**Integrating Social Links**\n\nI\'m making progress on linking all the official social handles, and now have the YouTube link solidified: `https://youtube.com/@oluwadamilolaolayinka-fk2ry`. I\'ve added the proper YouTube SVG icon, and I\'ll open all external social links safely in a new tab using `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`. The YouTube button will appear alongside Email, Phone, and WhatsApp in the Production Enquiry Section. I\'ve also re-emphasized that I will not fabricate any content like video details, views, or client specifics, just a direct link.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
