    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "## FINAL VISUAL QUALITY CONTROL \342\200\224 ENTERTAINMENT + LUXURY\n\nThe tonal refinement is now heading in the right direction.\n\nBefore considering the D1 Streams website visually complete, perform one final design-quality pass.\n\nThe objective is to make sure the website feels like a **premium international entertainment, live-event and broadcast production company**, rather than simply a dark/light corporate website.\n\n### 1. CHECK THE VISUAL ENERGY\n\nThe website should feel alive.\n\nUse the existing cinematic production photography to create a sense of:\n\n* Live events\n* Concerts\n* Performances\n* Large audiences\n* Stage lighting\n* Cameras\n* Production crews\n* Broadcast environments\n* Technical precision\n\nDo not let the light sections become visually sterile or corporate.\n\nThey should feel like **premium editorial pages**, not generic SaaS sections.\n\n### 2. IMPROVE IMAGE SCALE\n\nWhere an image is important, let it be large.\n\nUse:\n\n* Full-width cinematic images\n* Large editorial crops\n* Edge-to-edge photography where appropriate\n* Strong image-to-text compositions\n\nAvoid many small generic cards when a large cinematic image would create more impact.\n\n### 3. CREATE A STRONG LIGHT/DARK RHYTHM\n\nThe current palette should feel intentional.\n\nUse dark sections for:\n\n**Drama / Production / Performance / Broadcast**\n\nUse light sections for:\n\n**Information / Editorial / Process / Credibility**\n\nThe transitions should feel like part of the art direction.\n\n### 4. DO NOT OVERDESIGN\n\nLuxury does not require excessive effects.\n\nKeep:\n\n* Clean grids\n* Large typography\n* Generous whitespace\n* Fine borders\n* Sophisticated spacing\n* Subtle motion\n* High-quality imagery\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Excessive gradients\n* Glow effects\n* Floating shapes\n* Glassmorphism\n* Excessive rounded cards\n* Generic AI visuals\n* Unnecessary animations\n\n### 5. HERO SHOULD REMAIN THE STRONGEST MOMENT\n\nThe hero needs immediate impact.\n\nIt should communicate within seconds:\n\n**D1 STREAMS**\n\n**LIVE EVENTS. BUILT FOR BROADCAST.**\n\nThen visually reinforce:\n\n**ENTERTAINMENT + PRODUCTION + BROADCAST**\n\nThe hero image must remain clearly visible and cinematic.\n\n### 6. RECENT PRODUCTION WORK\n\nKeep the real recent production locations:\n\n* RCCG Jesus Palace\n* RCCG Zone of Resurrection\n* RCCG Peace Arena\n\nPresent them as **Recent Production Work**, not testimonials.\n\nDo not fabricate quotes or reviews.\n\nIf authentic production photographs are available, use them.\n\n### 7. YOUTUBE\n\nKeep the official YouTube presence integrated into the entertainment identity.\n\nUse a strong CTA such as:\n\n**WATCH THE PRODUCTION**\n\n**Watch D1 Streams in action \342\206\222**\n\nLink to the official YouTube channel provided by the client.\n\nDo not invent video information.\n\n### 8. CONTACT EXPERIENCE\n\nVerify that:\n\n* Email opens correctly with `mailto:`\n* Phone opens correctly with `tel:`\n* WhatsApp opens correctly\n* Instagram opens correctly\n* TikTok opens correctly\n* YouTube opens correctly\n* Production enquiry form actually delivers submissions somewhere\n\nThe contact experience should feel as polished as the visual design.\n\n### 9. MOBILE\n\nPerform a complete mobile visual review.\n\nCheck:\n\n* Hero cropping\n* Typography\n* Navigation\n* Images\n* Buttons\n* Section spacing\n* Forms\n* Footer\n* Social links\n* Contact links\n* No horizontal scrolling\n\nMobile should feel intentionally designed, not like a compressed desktop layout.\n\n### 10. FINAL BRAND TEST\n\nView the website from the perspective of an international event organizer.\n\nAsk:\n\n> \342\200\234Would I trust this company to handle the broadcast and production of my concert, conference, church event or major live experience?\342\200\235\n\nIf the answer is yes, the visual direction is working.\n\nThe final emotional impression should be:\n\n**CINEMATIC.\nCONFIDENT.\nPREMIUM.\nALIVE.\nTECHNICAL.\nTRUSTWORTHY.**\n\nNot:\n\n**BORING.\nTOO DARK.\nGENERIC CORPORATE.\nGENERIC SaaS.**\n\nDo not redesign the entire site. Refine whatever is necessary to achieve this final standard."
    items {
      text: "## FINAL VISUAL QUALITY CONTROL \342\200\224 ENTERTAINMENT + LUXURY\n\nThe tonal refinement is now heading in the right direction.\n\nBefore considering the D1 Streams website visually complete, perform one final design-quality pass.\n\nThe objective is to make sure the website feels like a **premium international entertainment, live-event and broadcast production company**, rather than simply a dark/light corporate website.\n\n### 1. CHECK THE VISUAL ENERGY\n\nThe website should feel alive.\n\nUse the existing cinematic production photography to create a sense of:\n\n* Live events\n* Concerts\n* Performances\n* Large audiences\n* Stage lighting\n* Cameras\n* Production crews\n* Broadcast environments\n* Technical precision\n\nDo not let the light sections become visually sterile or corporate.\n\nThey should feel like **premium editorial pages**, not generic SaaS sections.\n\n### 2. IMPROVE IMAGE SCALE\n\nWhere an image is important, let it be large.\n\nUse:\n\n* Full-width cinematic images\n* Large editorial crops\n* Edge-to-edge photography where appropriate\n* Strong image-to-text compositions\n\nAvoid many small generic cards when a large cinematic image would create more impact.\n\n### 3. CREATE A STRONG LIGHT/DARK RHYTHM\n\nThe current palette should feel intentional.\n\nUse dark sections for:\n\n**Drama / Production / Performance / Broadcast**\n\nUse light sections for:\n\n**Information / Editorial / Process / Credibility**\n\nThe transitions should feel like part of the art direction.\n\n### 4. DO NOT OVERDESIGN\n\nLuxury does not require excessive effects.\n\nKeep:\n\n* Clean grids\n* Large typography\n* Generous whitespace\n* Fine borders\n* Sophisticated spacing\n* Subtle motion\n* High-quality imagery\n\nAvoid:\n\n* Excessive gradients\n* Glow effects\n* Floating shapes\n* Glassmorphism\n* Excessive rounded cards\n* Generic AI visuals\n* Unnecessary animations\n\n### 5. HERO SHOULD REMAIN THE STRONGEST MOMENT\n\nThe hero needs immediate impact.\n\nIt should communicate within seconds:\n\n**D1 STREAMS**\n\n**LIVE EVENTS. BUILT FOR BROADCAST.**\n\nThen visually reinforce:\n\n**ENTERTAINMENT + PRODUCTION + BROADCAST**\n\nThe hero image must remain clearly visible and cinematic.\n\n### 6. RECENT PRODUCTION WORK\n\nKeep the real recent production locations:\n\n* RCCG Jesus Palace\n* RCCG Zone of Resurrection\n* RCCG Peace Arena\n\nPresent them as **Recent Production Work**, not testimonials.\n\nDo not fabricate quotes or reviews.\n\nIf authentic production photographs are available, use them.\n\n### 7. YOUTUBE\n\nKeep the official YouTube presence integrated into the entertainment identity.\n\nUse a strong CTA such as:\n\n**WATCH THE PRODUCTION**\n\n**Watch D1 Streams in action \342\206\222**\n\nLink to the official YouTube channel provided by the client.\n\nDo not invent video information.\n\n### 8. CONTACT EXPERIENCE\n\nVerify that:\n\n* Email opens correctly with `mailto:`\n* Phone opens correctly with `tel:`\n* WhatsApp opens correctly\n* Instagram opens correctly\n* TikTok opens correctly\n* YouTube opens correctly\n* Production enquiry form actually delivers submissions somewhere\n\nThe contact experience should feel as polished as the visual design.\n\n### 9. MOBILE\n\nPerform a complete mobile visual review.\n\nCheck:\n\n* Hero cropping\n* Typography\n* Navigation\n* Images\n* Buttons\n* Section spacing\n* Forms\n* Footer\n* Social links\n* Contact links\n* No horizontal scrolling\n\nMobile should feel intentionally designed, not like a compressed desktop layout.\n\n### 10. FINAL BRAND TEST\n\nView the website from the perspective of an international event organizer.\n\nAsk:\n\n> \342\200\234Would I trust this company to handle the broadcast and production of my concert, conference, church event or major live experience?\342\200\235\n\nIf the answer is yes, the visual direction is working.\n\nThe final emotional impression should be:\n\n**CINEMATIC.\nCONFIDENT.\nPREMIUM.\nALIVE.\nTECHNICAL.\nTRUSTWORTHY.**\n\nNot:\n\n**BORING.\nTOO DARK.\nGENERIC CORPORATE.\nGENERIC SaaS.**\n\nDo not redesign the entire site. Refine whatever is necessary to achieve this final standard."
    }
  }
}
